[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C actually branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis E — entry point.** The `.so` exports five symbols. `driver.h` declares
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m only `driver()`, but the other four have external linkage and are therefore part
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m of the ABI surface a real consumer can (and the test harness does) call
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m directly. The call hierarchy, lowest level first:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m printLine(const char*)      <- leaf, null-guarded
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m printIntLine(int)           <- leaf, unguarded
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m bad(float)                  -> printIntLine
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m goodG2B(void)     [static]  -> printIntLine        (constant divisor 2.0F)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m goodB2G(float)    [static]  -> printIntLine | printLine
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m good(float)                 -> goodG2B, goodB2G
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m driver(float,float)         -> printLine, good, printLine, printLine, bad, printLine
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Tests exercise the leaves (`printLine`, `printIntLine`) directly, then `bad`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m then `good` (which is the only way to reach the two `static` functions), then the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m composed `driver` — not just the top-level convenience entry point.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis P — pointer shape** (`printLine` only): NULL / empty string / short ASCII
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m / long string (>4 KiB, crosses the stdio buffer) / string containing `%d`,
